maya: hey infra — quick heads up, I'm planning a small infra tweak for staging: scale catalog-statefulset replicas 3 -> 2 to free up one node for a perf run. I'll also relax the startupProbe timeout because we've been seeing spurious failures on cold starts. Opening a TF plan in a bit, wanted quick checks before I send a PR. cc @kevin @li :wave:

kevin: quick Q — is this the statefulset with RWO PVCs? scaling down a sts can orphan the highest ordinal pod, which may have unique data. we should either: do a controlled partitioned rollout (set .spec.updateStrategy.rollingUpdate.partition=1) or snapshot/migrate PVCs first. :thinking:

li: agree with kevin. also check resources: last time we saw slow shutdowns because terminationGracePeriodSeconds was 10s and it couldn't flush caches. bump to 60s for that app. maybe also increase startupProbe failureThreshold to 10 for long JIT steps.

josh: ping on PR when you have it — will do a quick CR. also, do we have HPA enabled for staging for this? if hpa is on scale-down might be confusing.

maya: good catches — HPA is disabled in this staging cluster for that app. here's the diff I'm going to apply in TF and k8s manifest (will push PR shortly):

maya: ```hcl
resource "kubernetes_stateful_set" "catalog" {
  metadata { name = "catalog-sts" }
  spec {
    replicas = 2
    update_strategy {
      type = "RollingUpdate"
      rolling_update { partition = 1 }
    }
    template {
      spec {
        containers {
          name = "catalog"
          resources {
            limits = { cpu = "500m" memory = "1Gi" }
            requests = { cpu = "200m" memory = "512Mi" }
          }
          startup_probe {
            failure_threshold = 10
            period_seconds = 10
            http_get { path = "/healthz/start" port = 8080 }
          }
        }
      }
    }
    volume_claim_templates {
      metadata { name = "data" }
      spec { access_modes = ["ReadWriteOnce"] }
    }
  }
}
```

kevin: that looks safe if you're doing partitioned rollout and keeping partition=1 for the canary. also make sure TF doesn't try to recreate PVCs — volume_claim_templates mustn't change or it will try to replace. check plan for "create" on pvc names.

infra-bot: terraform plan: 1 to update, 0 to add, 0 to destroy. Proposed: kubernetes_stateful_set.catalog: "~" -> updated (replicas, update_strategy, startup_probe)

sara: can we run a 10% canary (i.e., partition=1) for 30m then promote? want to watch cache warmup / latency p95. if all good, proceed to set partition=0 to finish. :eyes:

maya: sounds good — I'll create the PR with canary window notes and a runbook snippet for rollback. PR: https://github.com/redwood-inference/infra/compare/refs/pull/342 — includes TF and k8s manifest. triggering pipeline now. :white_check_mark:

deploy-bot: deploy pipeline started for PR #342 — apply in staging. status: running jobs (plan -> apply)

deploy-bot: deploy pipeline success — staging apply complete. partitioned rollout applied (partition=1), replicas now 2, startupProbe updated. monitoring for 30m per canary window. :rocket:
